---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Rest Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Rest Easy - Sleep Sounds iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/rest-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Rest Easy?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Rest%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I mix multiple sounds?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">On the mixer, tap a sound to start it, then tap more to layer them, up to four. Each sound in the mix has its own volume slider. Tap a sound again to take it out.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I set a sleep timer?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Tap the timer button at the top right of the mixer, choose how long the sounds play and how long the fade at the end takes, then tap Start. The sounds fade out gently, then pause, and your mix stays ready for the next night.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Will the sounds play all night?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Without a sleep timer, the sounds keep playing with your screen locked or while you use other apps. Taking out your headphones pauses them, so they don't suddenly play from the speaker.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does the app work offline?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Every sound is made on your iPhone as it plays, so there's nothing to download and no internet connection is needed.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I save my favorite sound combinations?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Build a mix and tap the save button next to Play on the mixer. Your presets appear on the mixer, in the menu and in Presets. Rest Easy also keeps your last mix, paused, for next time. To put a preset on the Home Screen widget, touch and hold it in Presets and choose Show on the widget.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can music or a podcast play at the same time?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. In Settings, turn on Play alongside other apps. Rest Easy then plays under your other audio, but its controls can't appear on the Lock Screen or in Control Center.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Why isn't there an Apple Watch app?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Rest Easy is designed for bedtime use when your phone is typically nearby. The Watch app wasn't a priority, but we may add it in a future update if there's demand.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
